# Font Awesome Pro lives on its own registry, which needs the account token.
#
# The token is deliberately NOT in this file. It is read from the environment,
# which is what Font Awesome's own docs recommend and the only reason this file
# is safe to commit: "Using environment variables for your token is a way to
# keep from checking it in to your source code repository."
#
# Set FONTAWESOME_NPM_AUTH_TOKEN before installing. Without it, npm install
# fails loudly on the Pro packages rather than silently resolving something else.
@awesome.me:registry=https://npm.fontawesome.com/
@fortawesome:registry=https://npm.fontawesome.com/
//npm.fontawesome.com/:_authToken=${FONTAWESOME_NPM_AUTH_TOKEN}
